CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: an unused non-virtual member function shall not be
implicitly instantiated.  Under Option B (on-odr-use instantiation) unused()
is never instantiated, so its assertion "must never appear" does not enter the
goto program and the forbidden pattern must be absent.

This is the precise lazy-vs-eager discriminator: unlike the other
cpp17_lazy_inst_* guards (whose ill-formed bodies merely get their conversion
error swallowed), here instantiation of the unused body would be observable in
the output.  It was KNOWNBUG while CBMC instantiated unused member bodies
eagerly; it became CORE once lazy on-odr-use instantiation landed.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md.
